  "body": "Stacked on #1804 (merge #1804 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nThe program simulation credits an earlier setup's declared edge breaks and marks before retaining its gouges.\nThis applies before a new block and before a side-on turn.\nThe credit uses only operations already cut in the departing setup.\nReal cuts below the declared finish surface still count as gouges.\nThe retained verdict keeps its matching display lattice without consuming the stock.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe walk judged the earlier stock against the sharp model.\nOnly the final verdict applied the operation's break and mark credits.\nAn intentional cut could therefore remain in the retained gouge count.\n\n## Tests\n\nEffort: high (not escalated).\n\nThe new `setup_carry_credits` suite passes all six pins:\n\n- `earlier_breaks_are_credited_before_a_new_block`\n- `earlier_marks_are_credited_before_a_new_block`\n- `earlier_breaks_are_credited_before_a_side_on_turn`\n- `earlier_marks_are_credited_before_a_side_on_turn`\n- `real_gouges_under_earlier_breaks_and_marks_survive_both_transitions`\n- `a_mark_from_another_setup_cannot_credit_a_real_gouge`\n\nThe four credit pins and the excess-depth pin failed before the fix.\nThey also failed after restoring the unchanged #1804 parent files.\nRestoring the fix made all six pins pass.\nRemoving break credit made both break pins fail.\nRemoving mark credit made both mark pins fail.\nRemoving mark setup filtering made the three-setup safety pin fail.\nEach mutation passed again after restoration.\nThe exact `upstream/main` file restore failed to compile because #1804 changes `LatticeTurn` to `CarryTurn` and adds `side_on_note`.\nThe compatible #1804 parent restore supplied the behavioral mutation check.\nThe operation-prefix restriction and the separate break-filter call were not independently mutation-tested.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all three steps in 12.4 minutes.\nThe gate ran sim, motion and app suites.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nClippy first caught a test-only clone of a Copy value.\nThe corrected test suite passed again after that spelling change.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe merge-base diff contains no `.nc` or `.cl` changes.\nThe direct comparison with current `upstream/main` shows 21 files from upstream changes after the parent branch point.\nEvery one matches the unchanged #1804 parent snapshot.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe new credit pins use the column engine.\nThey do not specifically exercise a retained credit on the field engine.\nThe existing field and carried-engine suites passed in the gate.\nWindows, Linux, manual posted-output inspection, UI suites and release lanes were not run.\nA full-perimeter break visible in the final setup's silhouette can still read as a gouge there.\nThis change only fixes the verdict retained before the transition.\nThe side-on pins isolate a generated straight edge pass away from the new top.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1804 changes `stock_sim_carry::walk` at both retained-verdict calls.\nThis branch starts at its head `8d5a2420a2e9280fb80e07dcf9b97ecda25e2cde`.\nPR #1811 touches `walk` in the separate electrode-dispatch block.\nIt also touches `stock_sim_held.rs`, different functions; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Credit an earlier setup's declared chamfers, deburrs and marks before retaining gouges across a new block or side-on turn, while retaining real excess cuts.\n\nFixes #1806\n",
